Stage 2: chart renderer foundation + SSIM golden-file gate

replay-engine/src/replay_engine/stage2/

renderer.py
- Async render() function wrapping Playwright headless Chromium
- Two locked profiles (ninjatrader_1min_dark, tos_mobile_dark) per
  pipeline spec section 5.2
- Profile configs: background colors, candle styles (solid for NT,
  TOS-hollow for TOS), cloud colors per platform, viewport dimensions
- PlaywrightNotInstalled exception when browser binaries missing
- Note: requires `playwright install chromium` to be run once on the
  host before render() succeeds; deferred until user returns

lightweight_charts_template.html
- TradingView Lightweight Charts pinned to v5.0.7 via unpkg CDN
- window.renderChart(payload) callable from Python via page.evaluate()
- Renders candlesticks + 6 EMA lines (3 cloud pairs)
- TODO: filled regions between EMA pairs deferred until first
  golden-file SSIM iteration that needs it

golden_file.py
- SSIM comparator using scikit-image structural_similarity
- SSIM_THRESHOLD = 0.85, MAX_RENDERER_ITERATIONS = 5 per spec section 5.3
- compute_ssim, best_match, gate_passed
- GoldenFileRegistry maps profile to exemplar PNG paths

scikit-image added to pyproject.toml dependencies.

tests/test_golden_file.py - 12 tests:
- spec invariants (threshold, max iterations)
- identical images score 1.0
- very-different images fail threshold
- resize handles mismatched dimensions
- low-noise passes threshold
- best_match picks highest SSIM
- empty references raises
- gate passes when all samples beat threshold
- gate fails when any sample below
- registry resolves NT-profile and TOS-profile exemplars (skipped if
  exemplars dir absent on the dev machine)

Subtle bug fixed: imread(as_gray=True) returns uint8 (0-255) for 8-bit
PNGs while resize() returns float (0-1). Mixed dtypes destroyed SSIM.
img_as_float normalizes both before compare.

104 pytest pass total. Audit clean. 54 vitest still pass.

Stage 2 RUN remains halted until user runs `playwright install
chromium` (~150MB Chromium download) and verifies golden-file SSIM
against the 11 chart-exemplars.
